{"name":"Harp Strings","hex":"#cbd0d1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"harp","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A musical instrument consisting of a body and a curved neck, strung with strings of varying length that are stroked or plucked with the fingers and are vertical to the soundboard when viewed from the end of the body\n\nAny instrument of the same musicological type.","Any instrument of the same musicological type."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To repeatedly mention a subject, especially so as to nag or complain.","To play on (a harp or similar instrument)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harp"},{"term":"strings","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of string"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Collectively, the stringed instruments in an orchestra.","Conditions, especially undesirable ones."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strings"}],"entries":[{"title":"Harp","blocks":[{"text":"The harp is a stringed musical instrument that has individual strings running at an angle to its soundboard; the strings are plucked with the fingers. Harps can be played in either a seated or standing position. Most commonly, harps are made of wood and are triangular in shape. Some have multiple rows of strings and pedal attachments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Harp.png/330px-Harp.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harp","wikidata":"Q47369"},{"title":"String","blocks":[{"text":"String is a long flexible tool made from fibers twisted together into a single strand, or from multiple such strands which are in turn twisted together. String is used to tie, bind, or hang other objects. It is also used as a material to make things, such as textiles, and in arts and crafts. String is a simple tool, and its use by humans is known to have been developed tens of thousands of years ago. String may also be a component in other tools, and in devices as diverse as weapons, musical instruments, and toys. The ubiquity of string as a tool has led to conceptual and scientific uses of the term, including strings in computer science, cosmic strings, and string theory."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Length_of_string.jpg/330px-Length_of_string.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/String","wikidata":"Q11064354"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Range_of_harp.JPG/500px-Range_of_harp.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Range_of_harp.JPG/1280px-Range_of_harp.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Range_of_harp.JPG/500px-Range_of_harp.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARange_of_harp.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Egyptian_vertical_harp%2C_kneeling_harper.jpg/500px-Egyptian_vertical_harp%2C_kneeling_harper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Egyptian_vertical_harp%2C_kneeling_harper.jpg/500px-Egyptian_vertical_harp%2C_kneeling_harper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Egyptian vertical harp, kneeling harper[10]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEgyptian_vertical_harp%2C_kneeling_harper.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Musicians_portrayed_on_pottery_found_at_Chogha_Mish_archeological_site.jpg/500px-Musicians_portrayed_on_pottery_found_at_Chogha_Mish_archeological_site.jpg?utm_so